From e431bbdbc9cb5ae8c4ecf28580ac1cf336329564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:04:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] G2-EX: resident EWRAM trimmed to +8 B (the aura's
 recorder and the clip mask live in the scene scratch)

The aura's list set (with the pointer to the list being recorded) and the stage's clip mask moved into memory the
scene binds (the exorcism's scene scratch / the stage's own block); the saved gba_nodraw of a clip is the clip
box's fifth halfword; the stage's static state is reordered so it keeps its 12 bytes. GBA EWRAM .bss+.data
246,700 -> 246,708 B (15,436 B free), IWRAM resident +16 B (plat_rect's clip dispatch), the room group's overlay
slot +152 B (stage_clip_rect; 6,612 B of it free).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
